\textbf{Robustness}\t PIVOT-XR wins on the hardest combined slice (+0.4~pp over Base-FT) and recovers the multilingual accuracy lost by PIVOT-++.

\textbf{Efficiency}\t XR adds 4.4\% parameters on the toy model, projecting to $\approx1.1$\% at 8~B. Latency increases by 0.3~ms (under 2\% projected). Peak GPU memory is unchanged.

\textbf{AOR analysis}\t Learned $\hat{\alpha}$ values cluster near~0.5, yielding no head split on the small corpus; correlation $r\approx0$ and ablations are neutral.

\textbf{CLEA transfer}\t Retrieval@1 jumps from 54\% to 83\%, confirming that a rank-4 map can align foreign sentences.

\textbf{Limitations}\t Results are indicative; full-scale runs are needed for definitive claims. The quad-view loss can cause GPU OOM on laptops; enabling it only in the last 1\,000 steps mitigates this.

